---
import Adr from "../../components/Adr.astro";
import Excerpt from "../../components/Excerpt.astro";
import Layer from "../../components/Layer.astro";
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";
import PageLink from "../../components/PageLink.astro";
import Path from "../../components/Path.astro";
import Routes from "../../components/Routes.astro";
import Rule from "../../components/Rule.astro";

const AM = "server/src/iki_server/amounts";
const SVC = `${AM}/services.py`;
const MODEL = "spec/src/iki_spec/model.py";

const H = {
  short: "How much of a record is left, and every change to it",
  how: "Declaring an amount, movements, transfers and splits",
  rules: "Movement kinds, concurrency, arithmetic and adjustments",
  ref: "Routes, code and decisions",
};
const toc = [
  { id: "short", label: H.short },
  { id: "how", label: H.how },
  { id: "declaring", label: "Declaring an amount" },
  { id: "movements", label: "A movement and the balance" },
  { id: "transfers", label: "Transfers, pools and lots" },
  { id: "splits", label: "Splits into aliquots" },
  { id: "rules", label: H.rules },
  { id: "ref", label: H.ref },
];
---

<Layout toc={toc}>
  <Layer n={1} title={H.short}>
    <p>
      A type with <code>amount:</code> keeps how much of each of its records there is, in one unit.
      The core changes it only by its own operations: recorded when a record is made, then drawn,
      transferred, split into aliquots or adjusted. Each is an append-only movement with the signed
      change and the balance after it, written in the same transaction as the record's single balance
      row, which the database never lets go below zero. Arithmetic is exact: a quantity that can't be
      held exactly in the record's unit is refused, not rounded (<Adr n="0139" />).
    </p>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={2} title={H.how}>
    <h3 id="declaring">Declaring an amount</h3>
    <p>
      <code>amount:</code> gives the unit and, optionally, a concentration field that converts a mass
      asked of a volume; <code>material</code>, the reference naming what the amount is of; then
      the <code>follows</code> list, the records whose eligibility a draw also meets; then
      the <code>aliquots</code> type a split makes and its <code>aliquots_of</code> reference back; and
      lastly <code>whole_units</code> for discrete stock (<Path p={MODEL} sym="class Amount:" />).
      The <code>iki/inventory</code> tube keeps microlitres and follows its contents:
    </p>
    <Excerpt file="plugins/inventory/types/tube.yaml" start="^amount:" />
    <p>
      A unit must add up: a volume, a mass, or a count (moles among them, as UCUM defines them);
      percentages and parts per million or billion are refused. Conversions use UCUM's factors as
      exact fractions, from Iki's own parser (<Path p="spec/src/iki_spec/validate.py" sym="def _adds_up(" />, <Path p="spec/src/iki_spec/units/__init__.py" />).
      A type with a registry identity has no amount:
      a molecule isn't a tube of it.
    </p>

    <h3 id="movements">A movement and the balance</h3>
    <p>
      Each movement keeps its kind, the signed change and the balance after it in the record's unit,
      what was asked for in its own unit exactly as given, the counterpart of a transfer or split, what
      a draw was used in and the source it followed, the code scanned, an operation shared by the
      movements of one request, and the person, agent, client, path and reason. Triggers refuse
      UPDATE, DELETE and TRUNCATE on it (<Path p={`${AM}/models.py`} sym="class Movement(" />, <Path
        p="server/src/iki_server/plugins/operations.py"
        sym="class AppendOnly("
      />). Each is also audited as <code>entity.amount_moved</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      The current amount is a stored row, the ledger's last balance, not a sum taken on read. The
      database refuses a negative one, and a negative balance on a movement too (<Path
        p={`${AM}/models.py`}
        sym='name="iki_amount_not_negative"'
      />). A statement trigger on movements adds edges to the record graph: <code>aliquot</code> and <code>transfer</code> from
      a record to its counterpart, and <code>used</code> from what a draw
      went into to what it was drawn from, so an experiment shows downstream of its tube (<Adr
        n="0123"
      />, <Path p="server/src/iki_server/graph/sql.py" sym="MOVEMENTS = (" />).
    </p>

    <h3 id="transfers">Transfers, pools and lots</h3>
    <p>
      A transfer takes from one record and gives to another in one operation, both quantities exact
      in their own units, or neither changes. Transferring into a record with a concentration rewrites
      the concentration to the pool's, as a revision whose reason names the transfer; it's unknown
      when the source's isn't recorded (<Adr n="0157" />, <Path p={SVC} sym="def _pool(" />). A transfer
      can't change what a record is: into a type with <code>material</code> goes only material of the
      same entity, and into a record a state locks, such as a released lot, only material in that same
      state (<Adr n="0162" />, <Path p={SVC} sym="def _what_it_takes(" />).
    </p>

    <h3 id="splits">Splits into aliquots</h3>
    <p>
      <code>POST /entities/&#123;ref&#125;/aliquots</code> makes up to 200 new records in the
      source's project, each holding the same amount, and takes exactly their total from the source:
      one <code>aliquoted</code> movement on the source and an <code>aliquot</code> movement opening
      each new record, under one operation. An aliquot is of what it was split from; it can't be given
      another material (<Path p={SVC} sym="def split(" />). A split tube is still inventory, and
      a result on an aliquot can count toward the tube it came from (<PageLink to="Release and completion" hash="completion" />).
    </p>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={4} title={H.rules}>
    <div class="rules">
      <Rule title="Movement kinds and draw purposes" open>
        <Excerpt file={`${AM}/models.py`} start="^class MovementKind\(" />
        <p>
          A <code>drawn</code> movement must have a purpose and no other kind may; only a draw can name
          what it was used in. Both are database checks (<Path
            p={`${AM}/models.py`}
            sym='name="iki_amount_draw_purpose"'
          />, <Path p={`${AM}/models.py`} sym='name="iki_amount_used_in_a_draw"' />). What a draw
          checks is on <PageLink to="Draws and samples" />.
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Concurrency and exact arithmetic">
        <p>
          Each operation locks its records, in key order, then their amount rows, in key order, so two
          transfers between the same records can't deadlock; a second draw waits and sees what's left
          (<Path p={SVC} sym="def _lock_records(" />, <Path p={SVC} sym="def _locked(" />). Amounts keep
          40 digits, 12 after the point; arithmetic runs at twice that with half-even rounding, so a
          sum or product of two amounts is exact (<Path p={SVC} sym="_EXACT = Context(" />). Each
          change moves the balance's timestamp forward by at least a microsecond, because that
          timestamp is the balance's revision (<Path p={SVC} sym="def _change(" />).
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Adjustments">
        <p>
          An adjustment sets the amount to what it was found to be, as a recount or a correction. It
          needs a reason and the balance revision the caller saw in <code>If-Balance-Revision</code>,
          or <code>unrecorded</code> for a record with no amount yet: without it, 428; stale, 409 <code>stale_balance</code> (<Path
            p={SVC}
            sym="def adjust("
          />, <Path
            p="server/src/iki_server/api/amounts.py"
            sym='alias="If-Balance-Revision"'
          />).
        </p>
      </Rule>
      <Rule title="Where the ADRs and the code differ">
        <ul>
          <li>
            An adjustment's <code>If-Balance-Revision</code> requirement is in no ADR; <Adr
              n="0139"
            /> asks only for a reason.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </Rule>
    </div>
  </Layer>

  <Layer n={5} title={H.ref}>
    <Routes tags={["amounts"]} />
    <div class="refs">
      <h3>Where</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><Path p={SVC} />: drawing, transferring, splitting and adjusting</li>
        <li><Path p={`${AM}/models.py`} />: the balance and the movement ledger</li>
        <li><Path p={`${AM}/stock.py`} />: a project's stock, from its lots' balances</li>
        <li><Path p="spec/src/iki_spec/units" />: UCUM units</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Decisions</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><Adr n="0139" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0157" title /></li>
        <li><Adr n="0162" title /></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </Layer>
</Layout>
